## Time as sensation

In drifting cinema, duration stops being a container and becomes the subject. A held shot is not dead time; it is the film asking you to notice what changes when nothing happens.

## The score underneath

Ambient scores do the narrative work that dialogue refuses. Listen to the room tone and you hear the plot: pressure, hesitation, the long exhale before a decision nobody narrates.
